# CR 702.177b's own example, with the exhaust ability begun first a mana ability (which never goes on the stack, CR 605.3a):
# Elvish Refueler and two Loot, the Pathfinders (the second a Spark Double copy). Turn 3: Loot #1's exhaust mana ability
# (RRR) and the Refueler's exhaust are used. Turn 5: Spark Double copies Loot and its exhaust mana ability is used. Turn 7,
# with an empty pool, Loot #1's exhaust mana ability is activated again under the Refueler's permission; while its {G} is
# being paid, Loot #2's exhaust mana ability, used before, is refused: an exhaust ability has begun to be activated this
# turn. Loot #1 cannot pay for itself either. A Forest pays the {G} and Loot #1 adds RRR.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Elvish Refueler
Forest
Loot, the Pathfinder
Spark Double
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
